committer Shaw <shawmakesmagic@gmail.com> 1792929260 -0700

Recover pump claim_token_incentives + admin_update_token_incentives (SDK hard-fail fix)

These two bonding-curve handlers were dropped from pump dispatch in a restructuring
(pump had 53 pub fn vs 56 IDL instructions), so @pump-fun/pump-sdk calls returned Anchor
InstructionFallbackNotFound. Recovered as genuine logic (from repo history 4b3d3dcb +
the implemented pump_amm twins, confirmed against the decompiled original wrappers) and
re-wired into dispatch, taking pump to 55 handlers.

New: programs/pump/src/incentives.rs (admin_update_token_incentives), programs/pump/src/
token_incentives/{mod,claim_token_incentives}.rs (claim_token_incentives). Wiring in
lib.rs (+6) and #[derive(Debug)] on GlobalVolumeAccumulator in volume_sync.rs (+1, for the
state log the oracle checks).

Validated on a fresh v1.43 build against evidence/original/pump/deployed.so (oracle only):
pump_claim_token_incentives_differential mismatches=[]; pump_admin_token_incentives_differential
target_successes==candidate_successes==44, mismatches=[]. Byte-identical behavior on every
watched field (accounts/state/events/errors/CPIs). No binary patching, no synthetic bypass.

